  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pamu Seshandra Kumar vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 6 July, 2022 Author: Ninala Jayasurya",
    "facts": "2. This Criminal Petition is filed under Section 482 of Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973 (for short 'Cr.P.C.') seeking to quash the proceedings in F.I.R.No.148 of 2019 on the file of VI Town Police Station, Nellore, SPSR Nellore District, registered for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 272, 273, 188 of Indian Penal Code and Section 59(i) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006( for short 'FSSA'). 3. So, he would pray for quash of the F.I.R., registered against the petitioners/accused Nos.1 and 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners/accused Nos.1 and 3 would submit that this is a covered matter in view of the earlier common order passed by this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch, whereby this Court has [LEAKAGE_MASK] several F.I.Rs registered for the similar offences based on identical facts. Therefore, he would submit that the petitioners, who are similarly placed, are also entitled for quash of the F.I.R.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners/accused Nos.1 and 3 would submit that this is a covered matter in view of the earlier common order passed by this Court in Criminal Petition Nos.5421 of 2019 and batch, whereby this Court has [LEAKAGE_MASK] several F.I.Rs registered for the similar offences based on identical facts. Therefore, he would submit that the petitioners, who are similarly placed, are also entitled for quash of the F.I.R.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
